  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  A closed, prospectively constrained evaluation of evidence-status overclaiming
  in a tool-using local language-model setting. The final E3-A run observed
  18/24 operational STATUS_OVERCLAIM events in forced-ambiguity cases; the model
  returned EVIDENCE_STATUS: SUFFICIENT in 42/48 responses overall. Post-closure
  semantic sensitivity analyses give F2 control success 4/6 instead of frozen
  0/6 and F3 control success 4/6 instead of frozen 0/6; neither family reaches
  the frozen 6/6 competence gate.
